						<h2
							class="font-headline text-2xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-bone-white sm:text-4xl"
						>
							What stays raw, and why
						</h2>
						<p class="font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
							Before any classification or storage, <code class="font-mono text-xs"
								>transform_tool_result</code
							> runs its skip gates: a result is left untouched when it is empty;
							when the tool is in the <strong class="text-bone-white">essential set</strong> -
							<code class="font-mono text-xs">skill_view</code>,
							<code class="font-mono text-xs">skills_list</code>,
							<code class="font-mono text-xs">skill_manage</code>,
							<code class="font-mono text-xs">memory</code>,
							<code class="font-mono text-xs">session_search</code>,
							<code class="font-mono text-xs">read_file</code>,
							<code class="font-mono text-xs">read_terminal</code>; when it is one of
							Aphrodite's own tools or a headroom helper; or when it sits below the
							tool threshold (docs/plugin/hooks.md:76-83).
						</p>
						<p class="font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
							The logic is not protectionism - it is information theory per surface.
							The essential tools return compact, self-describing metadata the agent
							needs raw: a skill's instructions, a memory entry, a file's content.
							Compressing them would trade precision for nothing. The self-tools are
							already the compressed form: their output is a marker or a catalog, and
							marking a marker is the preview-doubling bug in slow motion. And the
							size gate is the quiet one - most tool output is simply small, and
							passes through without a store entry ever existing.
						</p>
						<p class="font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
							One subtlety: file references are tracked <em>before</em> the skip gates,
							so <code class="font-mono text-xs">read_file</code> and
							<code class="font-mono text-xs">search_files</code> results feed the
							recall catalog even when they are never compressed (docs/plugin/hooks.md:92-94).
						</p>
					</div>
